  "verbalization": "Phyllofolactones F appears to be a target of multiple compounds that ultimately lead to VMRC-MELG through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Phyllofolactones F directly interacts with T-cell surface glycoprotein CD3, which is then targeted by two different compounds—2-(1a,4-dimethyl-3,3a,4,5,6,7,7a,7b-octahydro-2H-naphtho[1,2-b]oxiren-7-yl)prop-2-enoic acid and Lup-20(29)-en-3-ol, (3beta)-—both of which have VMRC-MELG as their target. This indicates a potential pathway where Phyllofolactones F may influence CD3, which in turn is targeted by these compounds, leading to VMRC-MELG. The evidence suggests a possible mechanism involving CD3 as a mediator, though the exact role of Phyllofolactones F in this process remains unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship between Phyllofolactones F and VMRC-MELG, emphasizing the need for further investigation into the molecular mechanisms underlying this interaction.",
